cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this audit or its Lean certificates, please cite the versioned release."
type: software
title: "A Lean-checked parameter audit for exact discrete Fourier transforms"
version: "0.2.26"
date-released: "2026-10-08"
authors:
  - name: "QZP"
abstract: >-
  Lean-checked arithmetic and local frame certificates for a parameter audit
  of the unrestricted-coefficient exact discrete Fourier transform recurrence.
  The release records finite-network and conditional research candidates and
  explicitly leaves the complete all-length frame-labelled recursion open.
  It also records the concrete Walsh-frame commutation lemma for orthogonal
  binary address changes, a nondegenerate one-coordinate projected-phase
  instance, a two-coordinate nested residual of rank one, and normalized
  Walsh framed-phase composition identities.  This version adds a formal
  q-free side-moment reuse identity, exact fixed-coordinate incidence-rank
  certificates, and an H18 local frame build audit.  This version additionally
  attaches the reuse identity to supplied finite-prefix frame schedules and
  parameterizes the fused-centre normalized arithmetic; these remain local or
  conditional certificates and do not by themselves provide a global gate
  schedule.
repository-code: "https://github.com/whyihaveyou/math"
url: "https://github.com/whyihaveyou/math/releases/tag/v0.2.26-general-fused-reuse"
identifiers:
  - type: doi
    value: "10.5281/zenodo.23235438"
    description: "Zenodo DOI for the preceding v0.2.25-nested-reuse-rank-audit archive"
license: "Apache-2.0"
keywords:
  - "exact discrete Fourier transform"
  - "linear circuits"
  - "Lean"
  - "formal verification"
  - "unrestricted coefficients"
